---
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Bench Log — Local AI, tested on real hardware</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #15130F;
    --bg-raised: #1C1913;
    --ink: #EDE6D8;
    --ink-dim: #A39C8C;
    --muted: #7C8577;
    --accent: #E8A33D;
    --line: #2B2820;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  body {
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  a { color: inherit; }

  header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 28px 6vw;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .wordmark {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }
  .wordmark span { color: var(--accent); }
  nav a {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-left: 28px;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }
  nav a:hover { color: var(--ink); }

  .hero {
    padding: 9vw 6vw 6vw;
    max-width: 880px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.4vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    max-width: 15ch;
  }
  .hero p {
    margin-top: 24px;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  .feed {
    padding: 2vw 6vw 8vw;
    display: grid;
    gap: 28px;
    max-width: 880px;
  }
  .section-label {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .entry {
    background: var(--bg-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 26px 28px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .stamp {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 2px;
    padding: 3px 9px;
    transform: rotate(-1.2deg);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .entry h2 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  .entry .meta {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .entry p { color: var(--ink-dim); max-width: 64ch; }
  .entry .read-more {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
  }
  .entry .read-more:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }

  .subscribe {
    margin: 0 6vw 8vw;
    max-width: 880px;
    background: var(--bg-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 34px 32px;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .subscribe h3 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .subscribe p { color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 0.92rem; max-width: 42ch; }
  .subscribe form {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .subscribe input {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink);
    padding: 11px 14px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    width: 220px;
  }
  .subscribe button {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #15130F;
    border: none;
    padding: 11px 20px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  footer {
    padding: 26px 6vw 40px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <div class="wordmark">bench<span>.log</span></div>
  <nav>
    <a href="#log">Log</a>
    <a href="#about">About</a>
    <a href="#newsletter">Newsletter</a>
  </nav>
</header>

<section class="hero" id="about">
  <span class="eyebrow">Local AI, tested on ordinary hardware</span>
  <h1>We test which local AI models and ComfyUI workflows actually run, then publish the exact configs.</h1>
  <p>A running log of real work: RTX 5070 Ti benchmarks, ComfyUI workflows, and local AI deployments for German and European creators and small businesses. Written as it happens, not as a review.</p>
</section>

<section class="feed" id="log">
  <div class="section-label">Latest entries</div>

  <article class="entry">
    <span class="stamp">tested · localki · pc1 offline</span>
    <h2>Why a tax advisor's Excel habit broke my RAG pipeline</h2>
    <div class="meta">24 Jul 2026 · FastAPI · ChromaDB · Ollama Qwen 2.5 14B</div>
    <p>Six bugs came out of a pilot session. One traced back to a habit that predates the software by a decade, and it was quietly destroying the document structure the whole retrieval pipeline depends on.</p>
    <a class="read-more" href="/log/localki-excel-chunking-bug">Read the full entry →</a>
  </article>

  <article class="entry">
    <span class="stamp">researched · localki / klarverk · not built</span>
    <h2>A client asked if I could train a custom model on their images. I didn't know yet.</h2>
    <div class="meta">21 Jul 2026 · Stable Diffusion LoRA fine-tuning · on-prem</div>
    <p>A client asked about training on their own images instead of the RAG setup. Figuring out whether that's even a real offering, and why per-image pricing is the wrong model for it.</p>
    <a class="read-more" href="/log/should-i-even-offer-lora-training">Read the full entry →</a>
  </article>
</section>

<div class="subscribe" id="newsletter">
  <div>
    <h3>Get the next entry by email</h3>
    <p id="subscribe-status">One issue roughly every one to two weeks. No spam, just what actually got tested.</p>
  </div>
  <form id="subscribe-form">
    <input type="email" id="subscribe-email" placeholder="you@example.com" required>
    <button type="submit">Subscribe</button>
  </form>
</div>

<footer>
  bench.log — a project of Klarverk, Zirndorf
</footer>

<script>
  const form = document.getElementById('subscribe-form');
  const status = document.getElementById('subscribe-status');
  form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    status.textContent = "Signup isn't wired up yet — the newsletter is waiting on Substack API access. Check back soon.";
    form.querySelector('button').disabled = true;
  });
</script>

</body>
</html>
